                    {
                        "translation_id": "a16169a5-cbaf-483c-bc71-779996de6ea1",
                        "source_entry_id": "58cbb79f-7124-36af-8585-44840462d793",
                        "source_sense_id": "8045e043-4de3-3453-b41b-8402e2f7b5bf",
                        "target_lang_word": "parricide",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parricide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93333a96-0685-3785-a06c-5f66c0efb3bf",
                                        "entry_id": "f5447311-63f9-3be5-aba5-dc9ee060f654",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who kills a relative, especially a parent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c736586f-b4ad-48dd-87d4-b6cc9cbe4572",
                                                "sense_id": "93333a96-0685-3785-a06c-5f66c0efb3bf",
                                                "text": "I told him the reuenging Gods, / ’Gainst Paricides did all the thunder bend […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e51eac8-4b97-33b2-80c7-166e78be1a0d",
                                        "entry_id": "f5447311-63f9-3be5-aba5-dc9ee060f654",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who commits treason."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "parricide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "803df848-85f6-3754-aaaf-3066a603c1ae",
                                        "entry_id": "3ff7b3ee-e2ae-3553-a9a4-e1207bf62d91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The killing of a relative, especially a parent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2732c8ec-e887-4c4d-8ac2-dc3e3db2d4ef",
                                                "sense_id": "803df848-85f6-3754-aaaf-3066a603c1ae",
                                                "text": "The new accusation brought by Urban against Manfred of murdering his sister-in-law's embassador – it may be observed that, tacitly, he acquits him of parricide, fratricide, and nepoticide – requires a little explanation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "840bde69-53ca-47c7-a7c5-44f3f414afeb",
                                                "sense_id": "803df848-85f6-3754-aaaf-3066a603c1ae",
                                                "text": "The production of Schiller’s ‘Don Carlos’ was long forbidden, because Don Carlos loved his stepmother; in ‘The Robbers,’ the Father was turned into an uncle, and a stupendous effect was produced by the cry of “Unclecide,” substituted for Parricide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34cf5316-db30-3197-b0ed-b8c89aaba377",
                                        "entry_id": "3ff7b3ee-e2ae-3553-a9a4-e1207bf62d91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The killing of a ruler, or other authority figure; treason."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1885ef5d-c278-43e0-a158-276666d01d0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "58cbb79f-7124-36af-8585-44840462d793",
                        "source_sense_id": "8045e043-4de3-3453-b41b-8402e2f7b5bf",
